## 7. UI placement and copy

### Account setup / Profile → Privacy and personalization

Use an optional card after age range; never block basic use:

> **Private context for safer, more relevant information**  
> These optional choices are private. They are not shown on your profile or shared with businesses, creators, circles, or other members. You can change them anytime.

Place four fields in this order: age range, sex assigned at birth (optional), gender identity (optional), pronouns (optional), then the two purpose toggles with clear descriptions.

The `allowMedicallyRelevantContext` toggle copy:

> **Use my private sex-assigned-at-birth selection only when I ask a medically relevant question.**  
> We will not use it for recommendations, ads, business matching, or public profile information.

The `allowPronounAwareLanguage` toggle copy:

> **Use my pronouns in Kinfolk’s language when appropriate.**

### Prohibited UI

Do not display these fields on Profile public view, business pages, community cards, safety report cards, creator cards, Circle member lists, events, marketplace, or lead forms. Do not make a business owner ask a member for demographic context.

